ands remain available after each issue.                                 \n                                                                              \n  Add batch so operations can obtain the notices scheduled for one day under  \n  the current customer-facing behavior. Request:                              \n  {\"command\":\"batch\",\"on\":\"YYYY-MM-DD\",\"accounts\":[ACCOUNT,...]}. Response:   \n  {\"on\":\"YYYY-MM-DD\",\"notices\":[NOTICE,...],\"total_due_cents\":N}.             \n                                                                              \n  Include an account exactly when the send_on that the current notice command \n  would return equals on. Preserve input order and duplicate IDs among        \n  included accounts. Return the complete current notice object for each       \n  included account. total_due_cents is the sum of their amount_due_cents.     \n  Empty results return notices=[] and total_due_cents=0. Copy on unchanged.   \n                                                                              \n  Example input: {\"command\":\"batch\",\"on\":\"2026-04-                            \n  01\",\"accounts\":[{\"customer_id\":\"M-17\",\"renewal_on\":\"2026-04-                \n  15\",\"plan_cents\":19999,\"completed_years\":3,\"autopay\":false},{\"customer_id\":\"\n  M-18\",\"renewal_on\":\"2026-04-                                                \n  16\",\"plan_cents\":10000,\"completed_years\":9,\"autopay\":true}]}                \n  Example output: {\"on\":\"2026-04-01\",\"notices\":[{\"customer_id\":\"M-            \n  17\",\"send_on\":\"2026-04-                                                     \n  01\",\"credit_cents\":2999,\"amount_due_cents\":17000}],\"total_due_cents\":17000} \n\n\n\n",
